 and actor  lenny kravitz  though momoa started to make a name for  himself in film and television when he  was just a teenager  it wasn't until 2011 that he first  gained mainstream attention  that was when he burst onto the scene as  carl drogo on hbo's game of thrones  up until that point mamoa was generally  known for playing less  savage characters so he knew that he'd  have to do something impressive to land  the role  in an interview with the new york times  mamoa explained that drogo was a tough  character to portray  the leader of the dothraki is a man of  few words so momoa knew he would have to  demonstrate his powerful energy in a  different way  when he showed up for his audition he  decided to begin with a haka a maori war  dance  he hoped to show that he had the ability  to be as physically impressive  as the rule needed his heart was beating  so fast afterward that the rest of the  audition was difficult but he apparently  made enough of an impression to land the  role that changed  his life while momoa broke into the  mainstream as call drogo  his biggest role to date is probably in  the dc cinematic universe  where he plays aquaman the dc films  generally aren't met with quite the  universal praise that the marvel  cinematic universe  is but the film featuring momoa's turn  as the ruler of the seas  is regarded as one of the best films  that dc has put out  but before he became aquaman also known  as arthur  curry mamoa actually had several other  roles where he spent a lot of time  in the surf he grew up in hawaii and had  a successful career as a model before  auditioning for baywatch  where he played a young lifeguard named  jason until the series went off the air  he even returned for the tv movie  baywatch  hawaiian wedding mamoa also had a lead  role on north shore a series about an  exclusive resort hotel which was also  set in hawaii  aquaman wasn't even the first time mamoa  had been to atlantis he played run on  decks on stargate atlantis for several  seasons  which is probably the job that started  garnering him more attention before he  landed high-profile roles  and conan the barbarian and game of  thrones  we tend to imagine that once someone  becomes a household name  they're financially set for the rest of  their lives unfortunately that's  oftentimes not the case  for proof look no further than jason  momoa mamoa had a few acting roles that  gained exposure before bursting into the  big time in game of thrones but while  drogo was a major character in the debut  season of that series  it's important to remember that momoa  was in fewer than a dozen episodes  it was also the first season of the show  before it gained complete mainstream  saturation so it's not like mamoa was  off making quoting crowns for himself  after his time when the series ended in  fact the opposite is true momoa has  stated that he was totally broke and  struggling to pay bills  the actor told in style i mean we were  starving after game of thrones  i couldn't get work it's very  challenging when you have babies  and you're completely in debt obviously  momoa and his family are in a much  better financial situation now as he's  hardly struggling to land major parts  in addition to his ongoing role as  aquaman mamoa is involved with plenty of  other big productions like dune  it seems he'll be a part of the a-list  for quite some time  and he doesn't need to worry about  keeping the lights on anymore  mamoa often has his shirt off for his  roles and that's not a fact that many  people are going to complain about  however  that can make it tough to tell how many  of his tattoos are real and how many are  added to give his characters  a bit more personality well if you're  wondering some but not all of the  tattoos you see on momoa's characters  are very real the most obviously real  one is often visible in his public  appearances mamoa has a tribal pattern  on his left forearm it's a tribute to  his hawaiian roots  and it